254
00:08:35,595 --> 00:08:37,864
- That way, I'd have a goal. - That's true. Like losing weight.

255
00:08:37,865 --> 00:08:39,625
Yes. That's why. That's the perfect example.

256
00:08:39,695 --> 00:08:40,734
Trying to lose weight...

257
00:08:40,735 --> 00:08:42,211
- after buying a small outfit? - Yes.

258
00:08:42,235 --> 00:08:43,675
You don't get to wear it in the end.

259
00:08:44,005 --> 00:08:45,865
(Feeling guilty)

260
00:08:46,365 --> 00:08:48,334
- You have good energy, right? - Yes.

261
00:08:48,335 --> 00:08:50,475
Give me some good energy of a lucky motorcyclist.

262
00:08:51,275 --> 00:08:52,374
Pass it and come back.

263
00:08:52,375 --> 00:08:53,944
My gosh. You can count it.

264
00:08:53,945 --> 00:08:55,514
- I'll come back at all costs. - Okay.

265
00:08:55,515 --> 00:08:56,844
- This is my third time. - Yes.

266
00:08:56,845 --> 00:08:59,315
- Let's not waste our breath on it. - Okay.

267
00:08:59,585 --> 00:09:01,985
- Sir, see you later. - Okay.

268
00:09:02,155 --> 00:09:03,995
Nothing could've motivated him more than that.

269
00:09:05,325 --> 00:09:07,125
- I'm feeling great. - Bye.

270
00:09:07,425 --> 00:09:08,625
I think he can pass it.

271
00:09:09,055 --> 00:09:10,095
He looks confident.

272
00:09:12,125 --> 00:09:13,765
My gosh. It's freezing.

273
00:09:15,495 --> 00:09:16,965
It was freezing that day.

274
00:09:17,965 --> 00:09:19,205
Gosh, it's cold.

275
00:09:20,335 --> 00:09:21,574
It's way too cold.

276
00:09:21,575 --> 00:09:22,875
(Fidgeting)

277
00:09:23,775 --> 00:09:25,474
(Putting on the helmet when he has no motorcycle)

278
00:09:25,475 --> 00:09:27,075
Put it on. That keeps you warm.

279
00:09:29,015 --> 00:09:30,075
It's warm now.

280
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:32,015
It's warm.

281
00:09:32,685 --> 00:09:33,884
My ears are warm.

282
00:09:33,885 --> 00:09:35,155
It was really warm, by the way.

283
00:09:36,785 --> 00:09:37,884
- This is... - You know what?

284
00:09:37,885 --> 00:09:39,605
It looks like someone stole his motorcycle.

285
00:09:41,625 --> 00:09:43,254
- I see. So... - So it's gone?

286
00:09:43,255 --> 00:09:46,125
You'd ride the bicycle to school, but walk back home.

287
00:09:46,795 --> 00:09:48,695
- I see. Because someone stole it? - Yes.

288
00:09:49,935 --> 00:09:51,035
"My motorcycle."

289
00:09:52,535 --> 00:09:53,634
My gosh. Seriously.

290
00:09:53,635 --> 00:09:54,735
Hold on.

291
00:09:55,435 --> 00:09:57,445
(Tapping)

292
00:09:57,875 --> 00:09:59,274
(Let me see.)

293
00:09:59,275 --> 00:10:00,445
Jongno.

294
00:10:01,515 --> 00:10:03,015
I'm in Jongno now.

295
00:10:03,885 --> 00:10:05,145
Jongno...

296
00:10:07,015 --> 00:10:08,855
- What's that? - The list of good restaurants.

297
00:10:09,085 --> 00:10:11,254
I have many folders of restaurants I frequent...

298
00:10:11,255 --> 00:10:13,424
sorted by area on my phone.

299
00:10:13,425 --> 00:10:14,895
Gangnam. Gangdong.

300
00:10:15,055 --> 00:10:16,825
Jongno. There are many areas.

301
00:10:16,995 --> 00:10:20,295
People ask me to share them, but I rarely do because...

302
00:10:20,835 --> 00:10:22,555
I don't want the restaurants to get packed.

303
00:10:22,895 --> 00:10:24,504
You've been to all of these restaurants.

304
00:10:24,505 --> 00:10:26,005
Of course. I've been to all of them.

305
00:10:26,135 --> 00:10:28,535
So you've been to 50 to 60 restaurants just in Jongno?

306
00:10:28,605 --> 00:10:30,725
The Jongno Folder has more than 50 or 60 restaurants.

307
00:10:31,175 --> 00:10:32,905
You must go to a lot of restaurants.

308
00:10:33,005 --> 00:10:34,514
You can't even buy that kind of information...

309
00:10:34,515 --> 00:10:36,014
- with money. - Right.

310
00:10:36,015 --> 00:10:37,015
(Feeling proud)

311
00:10:37,515 --> 00:10:39,744
(Where should I go today?)

312
00:10:39,745 --> 00:10:41,754
Yes. I should go there.

313
00:10:41,755 --> 00:10:42,755
(I should go there.)

314
00:10:43,055 --> 00:10:44,885
Nice. This is great.

315
00:10:45,125 --> 00:10:46,405
- It's a pasta restaurant? - No.

316
00:10:47,095 --> 00:10:49,855
(Smiling from ear to ear)

317
00:10:50,825 --> 00:10:51,895
Here I am.

318
00:10:53,065 --> 00:10:55,195
My love, Zia.

319
00:10:55,765 --> 00:10:56,895
Venezia.

320
00:10:57,165 --> 00:10:58,204
Gosh, it's freezing.

321
00:10:58,205 --> 00:10:59,264
It's so cold!

322
00:10:59,265 --> 00:11:00,434
(A western-cuisine restaurant)

323
00:11:00,435 --> 00:11:02,235
Look at the sign! Oh, my.

324
00:11:02,305 --> 00:11:03,305
Western-cuisine restaurants...

325
00:11:03,306 --> 00:11:04,344
- all have the same decor. - Right.

326
00:11:04,345 --> 00:11:06,275
But this restaurant is the real deal.

327
00:11:07,415 --> 00:11:08,415
It's so cold.

328
00:11:08,416 --> 00:11:09,696
(He walks down to the basement.)

329
00:11:09,775 --> 00:11:11,085
Hello.

330
00:11:11,345 --> 00:11:12,615
It's been a while.

331
00:11:14,155 --> 00:11:15,184
- Gosh. - How nice.

332
00:11:15,185 --> 00:11:16,514
(The old-school decor everyone still remembers)

333
00:11:16,515 --> 00:11:17,684
It's like a scene from a movie.

334
00:11:17,685 --> 00:11:18,685
So many group blind dates...

335
00:11:18,686 --> 00:11:19,984
- took place there. - The red bricks.

336
00:11:19,985 --> 00:11:22,295
A lot of families dined out at restaurants like this.

337
00:11:23,195 --> 00:11:25,994
Jongno still preserves the scenery of the past.

338
00:11:25,995 --> 00:11:28,994
In my opinion, it gives us the nostalgic vibe.

339
00:11:28,995 --> 00:11:30,395
I have many memories from here too.

340
00:11:30,835 --> 00:11:34,134
As for this restaurant, it opened 39 years ago.

341
00:11:34,135 --> 00:11:35,604
- My gosh. - Upon walking in,

342
00:11:35,605 --> 00:11:37,304
you see all these interior props...

343
00:11:37,305 --> 00:11:38,974
and feel the old vibe with the lights and all.

344
00:11:38,975 --> 00:11:40,445
It's taking a trip down memory lane.

345
00:11:40,675 --> 00:11:43,544
People come to eat here for romance and the vibe.

346
00:11:43,545 --> 00:11:44,944
It's one of my favorite restaurants.

347
00:11:44,945 --> 00:11:46,184
Sung Hwan really likes that.

348
00:11:46,185 --> 00:11:47,754
- He loves romance. - It's really nice. I do.

349
00:11:47,755 --> 00:11:50,084
Have you two been to a place like that yet?

350
00:11:50,085 --> 00:11:52,224
Actually, do you know this restaurant in Jamsil?

351
00:11:52,225 --> 00:11:53,354
It's called House of Pork Cutlets.

352
00:11:53,355 --> 00:11:55,154
My gosh, I love that place.

353
00:11:55,155 --> 00:11:57,194
I love that restaurant. You have to order...

354
00:11:57,195 --> 00:12:00,094
two rolls of bread and one bowl of rice at the restaurant.

355
00:12:00,095 --> 00:12:02,395
They bake their own bread. Their bread is so good.

356
00:12:02,665 --> 00:12:04,264
- You go there for the bread. - For the pork cutlet. No.

357
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:07,235
They butter the rolls and give you apple jam on the side.

358
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:08,734
Have the roll plain with the jam.

359
00:12:08,735 --> 00:12:10,204
- Then put... - Right.

360
00:12:10,205 --> 00:12:12,874
Right. Put the pork cutlet and the salad in the roll.

361
00:12:12,875 --> 00:12:16,645
I mix the rice with the leftover sauce at the end.

362
00:12:17,385 --> 00:12:19,784
You order the pork cutlet set. Then you get...

363
00:12:19,785 --> 00:12:21,354
I also order that. You get three pieces.

364
00:12:21,355 --> 00:12:22,454
- I always get the assortment. - Fried fish, hamburger steak,

365
00:12:22,455 --> 00:12:23,555
- and pork cutlet. - Yes.

366
00:12:23,755 --> 00:12:26,624
Do you know this restaurant called Dolmen Pork Cutlet in Songpa?

367
00:12:26,625 --> 00:12:28,394
My gosh. It's on my list.

368
00:12:28,395 --> 00:12:30,594
But that place doesn't offer the assortment set.

369
00:12:30,595 --> 00:12:32,164
- Right. - They only serve pork cutlets.

370
00:12:32,165 --> 00:12:33,894
- And they give you udon. - It comes with the udon.

371
00:12:33,895 --> 00:12:35,094
- That's right. - That's how I remember.

372
00:12:35,095 --> 00:12:37,234
You guys seem to know the history of all these restaurants.

373
00:12:37,235 --> 00:12:39,164
It's like elementary school kids memorizing subway stations.

374
00:12:39,165 --> 00:12:41,104
You sound like a writer for a food column.

375
00:12:41,105 --> 00:12:43,275
It feels like I've met my soulmate.

376
00:12:43,305 --> 00:12:44,944
It's amazing how they memorized all this.

377
00:12:44,945 --> 00:12:46,674
- Right. - Write about restaurants' history.

378
00:12:46,675 --> 00:12:48,074
- Seriously. - But the thing is...

379
00:12:48,075 --> 00:12:50,344
- You have the palate of a kid. - I do have the palate of a kid.

380
00:12:50,345 --> 00:12:51,584
There's a dish you don't eat.

381
00:12:51,585 --> 00:12:53,385
- I can't eat fermented skate. - Right.

382
00:12:53,485 --> 00:12:55,414
There's an amazing restaurant for skate combo in my neighborhood.

383
00:12:55,415 --> 00:12:57,684
The owner makes the wraps for you.

384
00:12:57,685 --> 00:12:59,084
Hey, I know that place.

385
00:12:59,085 --> 00:13:00,155
Right!

386
00:13:00,185 --> 00:13:01,794
- Where? - How did you know?

387
00:13:01,795 --> 00:13:03,524
- That place is super famous. - Where is that?

388
00:13:03,525 --> 00:13:04,864
- The restaurant owner... - Where?

389
00:13:04,865 --> 00:13:06,194
Makes every wrap for you.

390
00:13:06,195 --> 00:13:07,994
So you just have to open your mouth.

391
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:10,234
That's the best restaurant for beginners.

392
00:13:10,235 --> 00:13:12,364
That has to be the first restaurant to keep eating skate.

393
00:13:12,365 --> 00:13:13,764
- Sung Hwan. - It sounds like...

394
00:13:13,765 --> 00:13:14,874
he can eat everything.

395
00:13:14,875 --> 00:13:16,275
(They're soulmates starting today.)

396
00:13:17,545 --> 00:13:18,975
Whenever I come here,

397
00:13:19,945 --> 00:13:22,265
it feels like I'm traveling to the past on a time machine.

398
00:13:23,245 --> 00:13:24,285
Sir.

399
00:13:25,615 --> 00:13:27,015
Could I have the menu?

400
00:13:29,015 --> 00:13:30,525
Thank you.

401
00:13:31,755 --> 00:13:32,884
(Even the menu looks old-school.)

402
00:13:32,885 --> 00:13:35,055
The menu itself has an old-school vibe.

403
00:13:36,625 --> 00:13:37,864
He's busy.

404
00:13:37,865 --> 00:13:39,094
- Sir. - Yes.

405
00:13:39,095 --> 00:13:40,795
I'd like the pork cutlet...

406
00:13:41,465 --> 00:13:44,705
and the fish cutlet.

407
00:13:45,965 --> 00:13:49,375
(He's on his phone again after placing the order.)

408
00:13:51,345 --> 00:13:54,215
(Playing the practice video for the driving test)

409
00:13:55,775 --> 00:13:57,345
That's a difficult part.

410
00:13:58,285 --> 00:14:00,645
(He grabs invisible handlebars and moves his hands around.)

411
00:14:01,855 --> 00:14:03,184
Right. Visualizing it in your head...

412
00:14:03,185 --> 00:14:04,685
- is quite helpful. - It helps a lot.

413
00:14:05,355 --> 00:14:07,084
Turn. One and two.

414
00:14:07,085 --> 00:14:08,925
(While he's determined to pass the test...)

415
00:14:10,825 --> 00:14:12,065
Thank you.

416
00:14:12,125 --> 00:14:13,194
Are you taking a test today?

417
00:14:13,195 --> 00:14:15,535
Yes. I'm taking the test for the motorcycle license.

418
00:14:15,635 --> 00:14:17,605
- I'll pray for you. - So... Thank you.

419
00:14:17,735 --> 00:14:19,934
I just have to make sure I don't get nervous.

420
00:14:19,935 --> 00:14:21,104
Don't be nervous.

421
00:14:21,105 --> 00:14:24,275
My heart is pounding even right now.

422
00:14:24,705 --> 00:14:25,774
- So... - I'm sure you'll pass it.

423
00:14:25,775 --> 00:14:27,714
That's why I came to my favorite restaurant.

424
00:14:27,715 --> 00:14:29,674
- Thank you. - Thank you.

425
00:14:29,675 --> 00:14:30,944
He's getting a lot of good energy.

426
00:14:30,945 --> 00:14:32,015
That's right.

427
00:14:32,915 --> 00:14:34,054
(It instantly brings back old memories.)

428
00:14:34,055 --> 00:14:35,085
That looks good.

429
00:14:36,115 --> 00:14:37,115
Look at that.

430
00:14:37,116 --> 00:14:38,154
(Western-style fish cutlet and pork cutlet)

431
00:14:38,155 --> 00:14:39,455
This place looks good.

432
00:14:39,985 --> 00:14:41,654
You can't have the western pork cutlet without radish kimchi.

433
00:14:41,655 --> 00:14:43,615
(It comes with radish kimchi and pickled radish.)

434
00:14:43,655 --> 00:14:45,264
- Thank you. - Here's the dessert.

435
00:14:45,265 --> 00:14:46,894
Thank you. My gosh.

436
00:14:46,895 --> 00:14:48,364
He even cut the apples into shapes.

437
00:14:48,365 --> 00:14:49,964
- Isn't that so romantic? - Yes.

438
00:14:49,965 --> 00:14:51,664
Check out the toothpick wrapped with cellophane sheets.

439
00:14:51,665 --> 00:14:53,064
- The toothpick. - Look at that toothpick.

440
00:14:53,065 --> 00:14:54,874
- I haven't seen them in ages. - It's been forever.

441
00:14:54,875 --> 00:14:56,034
The toothpick with cellophane sheets.

442
00:14:56,035 --> 00:14:58,675
(After a brief reminder of the old days, )

443
00:14:59,575 --> 00:15:02,345
(he slices the cutlet.)

444
00:15:02,875 --> 00:15:04,714
(Amazed)

445
00:15:04,715 --> 00:15:05,915
That's a nice feeling.

446
00:15:07,185 --> 00:15:10,214
Seeing how the knife is going in nicely, I'll pass the test.

447
00:15:10,215 --> 00:15:12,324
- That looks so good. - That does look good.

448
00:15:12,325 --> 00:15:13,925
"You'll pass."

449
00:15:15,625 --> 00:15:17,925
(He cuts the cutlet while wishing to pass the test.)

450
00:15:18,625 --> 00:15:20,164
I cut everything at once.

451
00:15:20,165 --> 00:15:21,594
So I can keep eating.

452
00:15:21,595 --> 00:15:23,515
- So you don't have to pause? - Right, no pause.

453
00:15:26,105 --> 00:15:29,575
(He picks up a piece of the pork cutlet and eats it.)

454
00:15:30,745 --> 00:15:32,375
(Humming)

455
00:15:34,215 --> 00:15:35,645
Fried food tastes good in general.

456
00:15:35,815 --> 00:15:36,815
Even fried shoes would taste good.

457
00:15:36,815 --> 00:15:37,815
- Right. - Yes.

458
00:15:39,485 --> 00:15:41,384
(This time, he picks up the fish cutlet.)

459
00:15:41,385 --> 00:15:43,705
- The fish cutlet looks good. - Their fish cutlet is good.

460
00:15:44,025 --> 00:15:45,855
(Staring)

461
00:15:46,285 --> 00:15:48,124
- You're keeping the balance. - Of course.

462
00:15:48,125 --> 00:15:50,025
- You go back and forth. - I have to alternate.

463
00:15:50,195 --> 00:15:51,895
I have a long list of great restaurants.

464
00:15:51,995 --> 00:15:53,224
Let's check out a few.

465
00:15:53,225 --> 00:15:55,635
- Sounds good. - He likes to eat. Great.

466
00:15:56,365 --> 00:15:57,834
(Savoring the dishes while alternating between them)

467
00:15:57,835 --> 00:15:58,935
It's good.

468
00:16:00,875 --> 00:16:03,175
(Sighing)

469
00:16:03,505 --> 00:16:05,805
I must have only positive thoughts.

470
00:16:06,605 --> 00:16:08,645
(He has another bite while trying to be positive.)

471
00:16:11,685 --> 00:16:14,685
(He swallows his anxiety with the pork cutlet.)

472
00:16:17,985 --> 00:16:19,185
I already finished everything.

473
00:16:20,355 --> 00:16:21,994
You ate everything.

474
00:16:21,995 --> 00:16:23,275
- That's impressive. - That's...

475
00:16:24,195 --> 00:16:27,125
Now that I had your lovely pork cutlet...

476
00:16:27,565 --> 00:16:29,465
and fish cutlet,

477
00:16:29,635 --> 00:16:31,835
I'll come back with my license.

478
00:16:31,935 --> 00:16:34,674
- I'll come back on a motorcycle. - Sure.

479
00:16:34,675 --> 00:16:36,434
I'll say goodbye here.

480
00:16:36,435 --> 00:16:37,575
Sure. My gosh.

481
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:39,245
Bye.

482
00:16:39,375 --> 00:16:42,014
- Did you enjoy the food? - Yes. I always enjoy your food.

483
00:16:42,015 --> 00:16:43,814
Our restaurant spreads good luck.

484
00:16:43,815 --> 00:16:46,085
- Right. - I'm sure you'll have a lucky day.

485
00:16:46,285 --> 00:16:47,554
How romantic.

486
00:16:47,555 --> 00:16:50,015
She always says the sweetest things.

487
00:16:50,515 --> 00:16:51,585
Thank you.

488
00:16:52,185 --> 00:16:54,454
- Have a good day. - Thank you for coming.

489
00:16:54,455 --> 00:16:56,925
- I have a good feeling about this. - All right. Thank you.

490
00:16:57,125 --> 00:16:58,764
I bet you passed because you ate there.

491
00:16:58,765 --> 00:17:00,494
If you hadn't, you probably didn't pass.

492
00:17:00,495 --> 00:17:02,575
He must pass the test for the restaurant to do well.

493
00:17:04,605 --> 00:17:06,905
If you fail, you should go back and apologize.

494
00:17:09,305 --> 00:17:10,534
(Now that I got some good energy, let's go and pass the test.)

495
00:17:10,535 --> 00:17:11,675
Let's go.

496
00:17:14,575 --> 00:17:15,614
Thank you.

497
00:17:15,615 --> 00:17:16,914
(A taxi arrives at that moment.)

498
00:17:16,915 --> 00:17:18,115
Thank you.

499
00:17:19,515 --> 00:17:21,015
- Hello. - Hello.

500
00:17:21,955 --> 00:17:24,355
I'm actually taking the test for my license.

501
00:17:24,455 --> 00:17:26,954
- I see. - It's the motorcycle license.

502
00:17:26,955 --> 00:17:28,025
I see.

503
00:17:28,925 --> 00:17:30,454
I'm getting nervous.

504
00:17:30,455 --> 00:17:31,594
(Nervous and anxious)

505
00:17:31,595 --> 00:17:33,365
I haven't felt this nervous in a while.

506
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:39,265
Sir, is there a way to relax when you get nervous?

507
00:17:39,335 --> 00:17:41,035
Is the test that difficult to pass?

508
00:17:41,205 --> 00:17:42,935
Gosh, it's no joke.

509
00:17:43,175 --> 00:17:46,205
On my 1st try, about 13 people signed up.

510
00:17:46,375 --> 00:17:47,744
- Only two people passed. - Right.

511
00:17:47,745 --> 00:17:49,744
- Really? - It's really hard.

512
00:17:49,745 --> 00:17:53,114
I used to ride an MX125 back in the day.

513
00:17:53,115 --> 00:17:54,285
Where?

514
00:17:54,415 --> 00:17:55,854
You met a cool taxi driver.

515
00:17:55,855 --> 00:17:57,014
I lived in Sillim-dong back then.

516
00:17:57,015 --> 00:17:59,284
You couldn't see me apart from the motorcycle.

517
00:17:59,285 --> 00:18:00,354
I had to hunch over a lot.

518
00:18:00,355 --> 00:18:02,594
I didn't know you used to ride an MX125.

519
00:18:02,595 --> 00:18:05,264
- Yes. I rode an MX125. - It's every man's dream.

520
00:18:05,265 --> 00:18:07,734
All men have this dream.

521
00:18:07,735 --> 00:18:09,064
They dream of riding motorcycles.

522
00:18:09,065 --> 00:18:11,504
Everyone carries a sense of romance at heart.

523
00:18:11,505 --> 00:18:13,464
I almost died three times.

524
00:18:13,465 --> 00:18:14,805
- My gosh. - Yes.

525
00:18:15,375 --> 00:18:17,074
I can't ride that anymore because I'm scared.

526
00:18:17,075 --> 00:18:19,274
Right. People need to be aware of the danger.

527
00:18:19,275 --> 00:18:21,235
They must be careful when they're on motorcycles.

528
00:18:21,615 --> 00:18:23,014
- You can't go back after accidents. - Right.

529
00:18:23,015 --> 00:18:24,245
There's something about you.

530
00:18:24,315 --> 00:18:26,644
That's why everyone tells anyone with a motorcycle to be careful.

531
00:18:26,645 --> 00:18:27,915
There's a reason for it.

532
00:18:28,315 --> 00:18:31,725
Looking at your hairstyle, I can tell you had a wild past.

533
00:18:33,225 --> 00:18:35,325
Your hairstyle reminds me...

534
00:18:35,755 --> 00:18:38,025
- of Tony Leung. - Right.

535
00:18:38,825 --> 00:18:40,764
It's my first time having this much fun...

536
00:18:40,765 --> 00:18:42,694
while driving a passenger.

537
00:18:42,695 --> 00:18:46,235
My gosh. This is great. I love talking to you.

538
00:18:46,405 --> 00:18:48,504
- What a relief. - I don't feel nervous anymore...

539
00:18:48,505 --> 00:18:50,135
after talking to you.

540
00:18:50,735 --> 00:18:53,705
I'm almost 100 percent sure that I'll pass today.

541
00:18:53,905 --> 00:18:55,944
- Thank you. - Sure.

542
00:18:55,945 --> 00:18:57,514
(They arrive at the destination as they enjoy chatting.)

543
00:18:57,515 --> 00:19:00,544
- Sir, can I shake your hand? - My gosh. Thank you.

544
00:19:00,545 --> 00:19:01,714
- Thank you. - Sure.

545
00:19:01,715 --> 00:19:03,654
- I'll make sure to pass. - Thank you.

546
00:19:03,655 --> 00:19:04,685
Thank you.

547
00:19:05,425 --> 00:19:08,195
(I have a good feeling about today.)

548
00:19:08,995 --> 00:19:11,695
(Looking around)

549
00:19:11,895 --> 00:19:14,634
(Seoul Western Motorcycle Training Center)

550
00:19:14,635 --> 00:19:16,034
A training center for motorcycles?

551
00:19:16,035 --> 00:19:17,834
That's an indoor training center.

552
00:19:17,835 --> 00:19:19,935
Gosh, I didn't know there was a training center.

553
00:19:22,675 --> 00:19:25,204
It's a training center where you can practice...

554
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:27,815
your driving skills for the Class Two License.

555
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:31,915
I came here to practice my skills for the second time.

556
00:19:33,215 --> 00:19:36,285
(It's full of training motorcycles.)

557
00:19:36,685 --> 00:19:38,984
The test for the Class Two Small Motorcycle License...

558
00:19:38,985 --> 00:19:41,555
has four parts.

559
00:19:41,655 --> 00:19:44,194
I'd give anything to skip the first part.

560
00:19:44,195 --> 00:19:45,324
It's the curved course.

561
00:19:45,325 --> 00:19:46,595
That's the worst part.

562
00:19:46,995 --> 00:19:48,734
- There are two curved turns. - That looks hard.

563
00:19:48,735 --> 00:19:51,235
- Many people fail at that part. - Yes, a lot of people do.

564
00:19:51,305 --> 00:19:53,404
The second part is the S-curve course.

565
00:19:53,405 --> 00:19:55,034
The course is S-shaped.

566
00:19:55,035 --> 00:19:57,075
- That's more doable than you think. - It's doable.

567
00:19:57,775 --> 00:19:59,674
For the third part, I have to go straight...

568
00:19:59,675 --> 00:20:01,074
- That one is hard too. - on a narrow street.

569
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:02,644
- What? What's this? - You must pick up the speed here.

570
00:20:02,645 --> 00:20:03,645
That's the hard part.

571
00:20:03,745 --> 00:20:05,145
Lastly, for the fourth part,

572
00:20:05,315 --> 00:20:07,814
- I must drive in a zigzag pattern. - You can't fail that part.

573
00:20:07,815 --> 00:20:09,335
Then you shouldn't be on a motorcycle.

574
00:20:09,415 --> 00:20:11,254
Once I pass all four parts,

575
00:20:11,255 --> 00:20:13,954
I'll get this beautiful license for motorcycles.

576
00:20:13,955 --> 00:20:16,625
You're allowed to go off course once on this test.

577
00:20:16,795 --> 00:20:18,995
But starting with the second time, you're disqualified.

578
00:20:19,265 --> 00:20:20,465
Here you go.

579
00:20:21,465 --> 00:20:23,195
(Checking his driver's license)

580
00:20:24,335 --> 00:20:26,465
(I'll pass no matter what today.)

581
00:20:27,235 --> 00:20:29,074
(He's ready to practice his driving skills.)

582
00:20:29,075 --> 00:20:30,674
- You're practicing on your own? - You must be cold.

583
00:20:30,675 --> 00:20:33,044
- That's why I watched... - Oh, my.

584
00:20:33,045 --> 00:20:34,765
A lot of practice videos at the restaurant.

585
00:20:35,615 --> 00:20:36,714
It's freezing.

586
00:20:36,715 --> 00:20:39,385
(Let me go for a ride now.)

587
00:20:41,385 --> 00:20:42,614
I'm nervous.

588
00:20:42,615 --> 00:20:44,925
(Mounting the motorcycle with excitement)

589
00:20:46,755 --> 00:20:49,354
- It's a matter of mentality. - That's right.

590
00:20:49,355 --> 00:20:51,401
- It's a matter of mentality. - Let's not be nervous.

591
00:20:51,425 --> 00:20:52,425
All set.

592
00:20:53,195 --> 00:20:54,265
All set.

593
00:20:55,665 --> 00:20:58,405
(Revving up)

594
00:20:59,635 --> 00:21:02,335
(Full of excitement)

595
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,545
Sung Hwan, you look cool.

596
00:21:07,575 --> 00:21:10,015
(He carefully moves to the starting point.)

597
00:21:10,175 --> 00:21:11,615
(Raising his hand)

598
00:21:12,045 --> 00:21:13,215
They call your name.

599
00:21:13,745 --> 00:21:16,315
When they say, "Ku Sung Hwan," I raise my hand and begin.

600
00:21:17,755 --> 00:21:19,655
(Nervous)

601
00:21:20,685 --> 00:21:22,854
Cornering is the most important.

602
00:21:22,855 --> 00:21:23,954
Watching him makes me nervous.

603
00:21:23,955 --> 00:21:25,401
- I know. - There are lines on the floor.

604
00:21:25,425 --> 00:21:26,624
- He crossed the lines. - Gosh.

605
00:21:26,625 --> 00:21:28,864
He crossed the lines.

606
00:21:28,865 --> 00:21:30,625
(He deviates from the track from the start.)

607
00:21:31,305 --> 00:21:33,635
(The motorcycle shakes like his mentality.)

608
00:21:34,405 --> 00:21:36,705
(He'll fail the test if he crosses the lines twice.)

609
00:21:37,175 --> 00:21:38,245
For goodness' sake.

610
00:21:39,045 --> 00:21:40,104
- Oh, no. - What happened?

611
00:21:40,105 --> 00:21:41,745
- Scores will get deducted. - Oh, no.

612
00:21:41,845 --> 00:21:42,944
- Did he cross the lines again? - This won't do.

613
00:21:42,945 --> 00:21:44,784
It wasn't easy to avoid crossing the lines.

614
00:21:44,785 --> 00:21:46,344
- Start over. - You fail if you do it twice.

615
00:21:46,345 --> 00:21:47,445
- You fail. - You fail.

616
00:21:48,415 --> 00:21:49,885
I'm bad at cornering.

617
00:21:52,185 --> 00:21:53,385
I'm bad at cornering.

618
00:21:53,555 --> 00:21:54,955
The curved course...

619
00:21:55,255 --> 00:21:57,324
is the most important in the motorcycle license test.

620
00:21:57,325 --> 00:21:59,725
It's the first course you encounter.

621
00:21:59,825 --> 00:22:01,994
Once you pass the curved course,

622
00:22:01,995 --> 00:22:05,064
there's a 95 percent chance you'll pass.

623
00:22:05,065 --> 00:22:06,464
- That's right. - So that's the hard part.

624
00:22:06,465 --> 00:22:08,775
I failed the last two times because of the curved course.

625
00:22:09,475 --> 00:22:11,945
(Most people fail at the curved course.)

626
00:22:12,345 --> 00:22:15,545
I'm having a third attempt in order to get some practice.

627
00:22:15,945 --> 00:22:17,744
The speed is important.

628
00:22:17,745 --> 00:22:19,044
You can't go slow.

629
00:22:19,045 --> 00:22:20,144
You fall if you go slow.

630
00:22:20,145 --> 00:22:22,154
- You lose your balance and fall. - You lose your balance.

631
00:22:22,155 --> 00:22:23,284
That's the difficult part.

632
00:22:23,285 --> 00:22:24,424
- That's the worst course. - Yes.

633
00:22:24,425 --> 00:22:25,984
The hardest course is in the beginning.

634
00:22:25,985 --> 00:22:27,754
- That's right. - That's where everyone fails.

635
00:22:27,755 --> 00:22:28,954
- That's right. - I did that two times.

636
00:22:28,955 --> 00:22:31,294
Back in my days, 6 out of 10 people failed.

637
00:22:31,295 --> 00:22:32,295
- Really? - Yes.

638
00:22:32,296 --> 00:22:34,024
It's much harder than driving a car.

639
00:22:34,025 --> 00:22:36,264
- It looks hard. - It looks so hard.

640
00:22:36,265 --> 00:22:37,665
- Other courses are doable. - Yes.

641
00:22:38,965 --> 00:22:41,335
(I'll succeed in it this time.)

642
00:22:45,705 --> 00:22:47,204
- For goodness' sake. - Why are you going so fast?

643
00:22:47,205 --> 00:22:48,974
- Why do you keep... - You're going too fast.

644
00:22:48,975 --> 00:22:50,714
- Why are you getting angry? - I mean...

645
00:22:50,715 --> 00:22:52,214
- You lack the talent. - It happens.

646
00:22:52,215 --> 00:22:53,284
Why are you getting angry?

647
00:22:53,285 --> 00:22:54,484
- I... - Just quit it.

648
00:22:54,485 --> 00:22:55,485
- Already? - You lack the talent.

649
00:22:55,486 --> 00:22:57,614
- Just eat pork cutlet. - Why are you getting angry?

650
00:22:57,615 --> 00:22:58,954
Who drives that fast?

651
00:22:58,955 --> 00:23:00,655
Drive a mini car with Ju Seung.

652
00:23:00,885 --> 00:23:03,125
What are you talking about? I want to ride a motorcycle.

653
00:23:04,195 --> 00:23:05,365
For goodness' sake.

654
00:23:06,965 --> 00:23:08,735
(Sad)

655
00:23:10,065 --> 00:23:11,835
(He continues to practice.)

656
00:23:13,605 --> 00:23:15,074
- Why are you going so fast? - For goodness' sake.

657
00:23:15,075 --> 00:23:16,504
No. It's okay.

658
00:23:16,505 --> 00:23:18,975
- He's going too fast. - Slow down.

659
00:23:19,445 --> 00:23:21,244
- Slow down! - He's really bad at this.

660
00:23:21,245 --> 00:23:22,274
This is so frustrating.

661
00:23:22,275 --> 00:23:24,714
I think he should get some help.

662
00:23:24,715 --> 00:23:25,815
- That's right. - I know.

663
00:23:29,055 --> 00:23:30,114
(What?)

664
00:23:30,115 --> 00:23:31,185
What's this?

665
00:23:32,985 --> 00:23:34,025
What's this?

666
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:36,595
- Someone came. - Who's that?

667
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:40,260
What's this?

668
00:23:41,130 --> 00:23:42,270
Someone came.

669
00:23:42,730 --> 00:23:44,999
- Who's that? - It's an indoor training center.

670
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,100
Is that Jong Hyuk?

671
00:23:46,300 --> 00:23:47,910
- It's an indoor training center. - Yes.

672
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:49,510
(Jun Su, what's your dad's name?)

673
00:23:49,511 --> 00:23:50,739
(Lee Jong Hyuk)

674
00:23:50,740 --> 00:23:51,909
He's all grown up now.

675
00:23:51,910 --> 00:23:53,579
(As Jun Su's dad, )

676
00:23:53,580 --> 00:23:55,109
(he became the national dad.)

677
00:23:55,110 --> 00:23:56,480
- How cute. - He looks so cute.

678
00:23:57,510 --> 00:23:59,780
(Sung Hwan's close friend, Actor Lee Jong Hyuk)

679
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:03,090
Jun Su and Tak Su's dad, Jong Hyuk came.

680
00:24:03,220 --> 00:24:06,020
He said he had the Class Two Small Motorcycle License.

681
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:09,589
He said that he was a motorcycle expert.

682
00:24:09,590 --> 00:24:12,830
So I asked him for help.

683
00:24:13,730 --> 00:24:14,769
There are many options.

684
00:24:14,770 --> 00:24:16,370
- An instructor came. - Now...

685
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:19,540
- I heard that you failed twice. - Today, I'll have my third test.

686
00:24:19,770 --> 00:24:22,170
When you failed twice,

687
00:24:22,640 --> 00:24:24,209
- did you practice alone? - I practiced alone.

688
00:24:24,210 --> 00:24:26,510
I practiced alone and watched YouTube videos.

689
00:24:27,180 --> 00:24:29,780
- Didn't you attend an academy? - No. I did everything on my own.

690
00:24:30,250 --> 00:24:31,650
It's no wonder you failed the test.

691
00:24:32,380 --> 00:24:34,690
So I wanted to learn from you.

692
00:24:34,750 --> 00:24:36,119
Please take a look...

693
00:24:36,120 --> 00:24:37,820
- as I drive. - Okay.

694
00:24:38,190 --> 00:24:40,690
Please tell me what I'm doing wrong.

695
00:24:40,790 --> 00:24:43,559
The fact that you're trying anything is wrong.

696
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:44,830
He's a nagger.

697
00:24:45,100 --> 00:24:47,730
Don't joke around. I'm nervous about the test.

698
00:24:48,300 --> 00:24:49,730
Of course, you're nervous.

699
00:24:51,170 --> 00:24:52,540
Hey, you're going too fast.

700
00:24:53,100 --> 00:24:54,669
- I begin here. - I told you that you were fast.

701
00:24:54,670 --> 00:24:56,951
- I told you that you were fast. - He noticed right away.

702
00:24:57,340 --> 00:24:59,379
(Raising his hand)

703
00:24:59,380 --> 00:25:01,380
- What are you doing? - They'll call my name.

704
00:25:02,280 --> 00:25:04,320
I'm keeping everything the same for the simulation.

705
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:06,200
- Okay. Go ahead. - He only does that well.

706
00:25:07,280 --> 00:25:09,119
- Go. - Oh, no.

707
00:25:09,120 --> 00:25:10,290
- I... - You failed.

708
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:13,560
- You fail if you do that. - I told you that I was nervous.

709
00:25:14,090 --> 00:25:15,630
Why did you yell "Go" so loudly?

710
00:25:17,160 --> 00:25:18,636
(He keeps everything the same for the simulation.)

711
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:21,300
Won't he succeed in it right away since the instructor is there?

712
00:25:21,530 --> 00:25:23,670
- Go slowly. - Let's go.

713
00:25:24,540 --> 00:25:25,600
Look far ahead.

714
00:25:26,670 --> 00:25:27,670
You crossed the lines.

715
00:25:27,671 --> 00:25:28,710
Look far ahead.

716
00:25:29,370 --> 00:25:31,109
(He crosses the lines this time as well.)

717
00:25:31,110 --> 00:25:32,810
Keep going.

718
00:25:34,380 --> 00:25:35,980
- Did I cross the lines? - Yes, you did.

719
00:25:36,010 --> 00:25:37,710
- Even now? - I think so.

720
00:25:38,850 --> 00:25:39,920
You failed.

721
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:41,719
I think you're going too fast.

722
00:25:41,720 --> 00:25:43,019
- Am I going too fast? - Yes.

723
00:25:43,020 --> 00:25:44,520
Step on the brakes as you go.

724
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,460
Give me a demonstration.

725
00:25:46,890 --> 00:25:48,659
- Me? - Yes. I can't get...

726
00:25:48,660 --> 00:25:51,230
a sense of it when I ride the motorcycle myself.

727
00:25:52,930 --> 00:25:55,430
Just show me how you pass the first course.

728
00:25:57,200 --> 00:26:00,899
(The motorcycle expert decides to give...)

729
00:26:00,900 --> 00:26:02,239
(a demonstration.)

730
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:03,369
- Here I go. - Go ahead.

731
00:26:03,370 --> 00:26:05,540
- I'll show you how to do it. - Okay. Show me.

732
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:06,809
Wouldn't he do it with ease?

733
00:26:06,810 --> 00:26:09,080
He'd pass the test at once.

734
00:26:12,020 --> 00:26:13,020
(Shouting)

735
00:26:13,021 --> 00:26:14,050
What?

736
00:26:16,220 --> 00:26:17,750
(Staggering)

737
00:26:18,060 --> 00:26:19,620
- What's going on? - Where is he going?

738
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:21,960
Hey.

739
00:26:22,630 --> 00:26:25,200
(Jun Su's dad, where are you going?)

740
00:26:26,660 --> 00:26:28,270
- I mean... - What are you doing?

741
00:26:29,330 --> 00:26:30,770
I think I'll fail the test.

742
00:26:31,070 --> 00:26:33,340
(He turns off the engine.)

743
00:26:33,500 --> 00:26:34,670
What are you doing?

744
00:26:35,040 --> 00:26:36,710
(Embarrassed)

745
00:26:37,210 --> 00:26:39,810
Please watch me from the back as I ride the motorcycle.

746
00:26:40,540 --> 00:26:42,486
(He goes back to practicing before he loses the hang of it.)

747
00:26:42,510 --> 00:26:44,980
Slowly.

748
00:26:45,180 --> 00:26:46,750
Now, turn.

749
00:26:47,320 --> 00:26:48,449
- He did it. - Nice.

750
00:26:48,450 --> 00:26:49,689
- Well done. - It was so smooth.

751
00:26:49,690 --> 00:26:52,090
Now, turn.

752
00:26:52,790 --> 00:26:54,559
- There you go. It's okay. - Good.

753
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:55,959
- Does that get a pass? - That gets a pass.

754
00:26:55,960 --> 00:26:57,590
- Finally, he'll pass. - Good.

755
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:59,829
Jong Hyuk, I got the hang of it.

756
00:26:59,830 --> 00:27:00,860
Try it one more time.

757
00:27:01,370 --> 00:27:03,569
That's it. Good. That's smooth.

758
00:27:03,570 --> 00:27:05,399
I suddenly got the hang of it as if I was riding a bicycle.

759
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:07,570
That's smooth. Good.

760
00:27:07,910 --> 00:27:10,209
(Laughing)

761
00:27:10,210 --> 00:27:11,340
I got the hang of it.

762
00:27:13,380 --> 00:27:15,300
That's good. You're good at riding a motorcycle.

763
00:27:16,310 --> 00:27:18,750
- Look at this. I'm all set. - There you go.

764
00:27:19,120 --> 00:27:20,826
- I'm all set. There's nothing more. - There you go.

765
00:27:20,850 --> 00:27:22,220
That's good.

766
00:27:22,920 --> 00:27:24,550
After Jong Hyuk came,

767
00:27:24,690 --> 00:27:26,460
my driving improved a lot.

768
00:27:27,260 --> 00:27:29,690
In soccer, being a soccer player...

769
00:27:29,930 --> 00:27:32,100
and being a coach are two different things.

770
00:27:32,330 --> 00:27:34,770
I think Jong Hyuk does better as a coach than a field player.

771
00:27:34,970 --> 00:27:37,570
That's right. Not all coaches are good at soccer.

772
00:27:37,940 --> 00:27:39,469
- I'll get going now. - Okay.

773
00:27:39,470 --> 00:27:41,190
- Do another round before the test. - Okay.

774
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:43,510
- I'll say goodbye from here. - Okay.

775
00:27:44,940 --> 00:27:46,940
All right. I'm all set.

776
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:50,650
It's a good weather to ride a motorcycle.

777
00:27:50,950 --> 00:27:53,250
Hello. All right.

778
00:27:54,050 --> 00:27:55,649
You need to take the test when you get the hang of it.

779
00:27:55,650 --> 00:27:57,450
That's right. You need to take it right away.

780
00:27:58,990 --> 00:28:02,190
(Singing a tune)

781
00:28:02,560 --> 00:28:04,129
(Korea Road Traffic Authority, Seobu Examination Office)

782
00:28:04,130 --> 00:28:05,459
(The location of the final battle)

783
00:28:05,460 --> 00:28:06,860
I think I got my license there.

784
00:28:07,100 --> 00:28:08,400
Most people do.

785
00:28:08,570 --> 00:28:09,929
I think I saw this place...

786
00:28:09,930 --> 00:28:11,890
- when Lee Jung crossed the road. - That's right.

787
00:28:14,140 --> 00:28:16,440
You need to step on the yellow lines only.

788
00:28:16,570 --> 00:28:18,340
- Why? - I came up with that rule.

789
00:28:19,480 --> 00:28:21,279
- Hold on. - But you failed the test.

790
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:22,350
Yes.

791
00:28:26,150 --> 00:28:30,120
(I'll overcome the jinxes.)

792
00:28:30,220 --> 00:28:31,419
(Test registration)

793
00:28:31,420 --> 00:28:33,020
I remember getting my license.

794
00:28:34,520 --> 00:28:35,590
It was so nerve-racking.

795
00:28:37,630 --> 00:28:40,529
(He can't hide how nervous he is.)

796
00:28:40,530 --> 00:28:42,469
- You can go right away. - Okay. Thank you.

797
00:28:42,470 --> 00:28:45,840
(He heads over to take the driving test.)

798
00:28:50,170 --> 00:28:54,280
(Driving test center for small motorcycles)

799
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:57,550
(He arrives at the waiting room of the driving test center.)

800
00:28:57,610 --> 00:28:58,750
Why is no one here?

801
00:29:01,390 --> 00:29:04,120
(Rummaging)

802
00:29:05,860 --> 00:29:07,290
(Sighing)

803
00:29:08,890 --> 00:29:09,990
Now,

804
00:29:10,660 --> 00:29:12,300
people are arriving one at a time.

805
00:29:13,560 --> 00:29:15,570
(The test takers enter.)

806
00:29:17,600 --> 00:29:19,600
(Staring)

807
00:29:21,240 --> 00:29:23,239
Is it your first driving test?

808
00:29:23,240 --> 00:29:25,280
(Is it your first driving test?)

809
00:29:25,980 --> 00:29:27,279
- Yes. - Do you know him?

810
00:29:27,280 --> 00:29:28,980
No. I've never met him before.

811
00:29:31,250 --> 00:29:32,349
(He sits next to Sung Hwan.)

812
00:29:32,350 --> 00:29:33,420
How many times...

813
00:29:33,820 --> 00:29:35,320
have you taken the driving test?

814
00:29:35,690 --> 00:29:37,049
This is my first time.

815
00:29:37,050 --> 00:29:38,790
It's your first time. Have you practiced?

816
00:29:39,260 --> 00:29:42,430
No, I'm a strong man who doesn't need to practice.

817
00:29:43,060 --> 00:29:45,399
This has nothing to do with being a strong man.

818
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:47,659
- Didn't you practice at all? - No, I didn't.

819
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:48,699
Really?

820
00:29:48,700 --> 00:29:49,870
Then the courses...

821
00:29:50,200 --> 00:29:51,869
I'm sure they're all the same.

822
00:29:51,870 --> 00:29:53,140
I just need to follow them.

823
00:29:53,770 --> 00:29:56,540
I don't know if he'll do well or badly.

824
00:29:56,910 --> 00:29:58,810
But... Really?

825
00:29:59,010 --> 00:30:00,279
If I fail, I'll take the test again.

826
00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:01,450
(So cool)

827
00:30:01,980 --> 00:30:03,900
- He's very cool about it. - He has a good idea.

828
00:30:04,680 --> 00:30:06,619
He's a manly man.

829
00:30:06,620 --> 00:30:07,820
(The test taker is easygoing.)

830
00:30:07,980 --> 00:30:09,719
Do you know how to ride a motorcycle?

831
00:30:09,720 --> 00:30:12,320
- Yes, I have a moped license. - You have a moped license.

832
00:30:12,790 --> 00:30:15,359
I bet he rode 125cc motorcycles.

833
00:30:15,360 --> 00:30:16,590
I think he'll pass.

834
00:30:17,360 --> 00:30:18,900
I'll pass in one go.

835
00:30:19,100 --> 00:30:20,160
In one go?

836
00:30:20,860 --> 00:30:23,070
- He has so much confidence... - Totally.

837
00:30:23,170 --> 00:30:24,506
- even though it's his first try. - Yes.

838
00:30:24,530 --> 00:30:26,200
Let's stay positive.

839
00:30:27,040 --> 00:30:28,139
Let's do it.

840
00:30:28,140 --> 00:30:29,809
Is there a motorcycle you want to buy...

841
00:30:29,810 --> 00:30:31,440
after getting a license?

842
00:30:31,740 --> 00:30:35,410
I want the 2008 model of CBR600RR.

843
00:30:36,250 --> 00:30:39,050
That's incredible. I checked out CBR today.

844
00:30:40,150 --> 00:30:42,490
- You have a good taste. - Let's get CBR. Seriously.

845
00:30:42,850 --> 00:30:44,450
Let's get CBR. Seriously.

846
00:30:46,520 --> 00:30:47,759
Is he someone you know?

847
00:30:47,760 --> 00:30:48,789
- You guys get along so well. - No.

848
00:30:48,790 --> 00:30:49,929
Is he someone you know?

849
00:30:49,930 --> 00:30:51,306
(They get along as they've always been friends.)

850
00:30:51,330 --> 00:30:52,529
Where do you live, brother?

851
00:30:52,530 --> 00:30:53,999
I live in Gangnam-gu.

852
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:55,070
- Gangnam-gu? - Yes.

853
00:30:55,600 --> 00:30:57,969
- Alone or... - I live with my mom.

854
00:30:57,970 --> 00:31:00,400
Gosh, you're from the district with the best education.

855
00:31:01,070 --> 00:31:02,746
I might not look it, but I'm a filial son.

856
00:31:02,770 --> 00:31:04,110
I pay for rent.

857
00:31:05,710 --> 00:31:07,380
I got a job at the age of 20.

858
00:31:07,540 --> 00:31:09,480
I work as a car mechanic.

859
00:31:09,850 --> 00:31:11,950
- In what year were you born? - I was born in 2006.

860
00:31:13,150 --> 00:31:14,750
- Did he say 2006? - He's a baby.

861
00:31:15,820 --> 00:31:18,160
Brother, let's introduce each other.

862
00:31:18,460 --> 00:31:19,789
My name is Park Tae Hwan.

863
00:31:19,790 --> 00:31:21,119
- I'm 21 years old. - Park Tae Hwan.

864
00:31:21,120 --> 00:31:22,159
Yes.

865
00:31:22,160 --> 00:31:23,630
I'm Ku Sung Hwan.

866
00:31:24,030 --> 00:31:25,099
- Nice to meet you. - Nice to meet you.

867
00:31:25,100 --> 00:31:26,629
- Both names end with Hwan. - Hwan.

868
00:31:26,630 --> 00:31:29,630
We'll pass thanks to the good energy.

869
00:31:30,030 --> 00:31:32,170
We'll pass no matter what. It's bound to happen.

870
00:31:33,840 --> 00:31:36,310
- If you pass... - Okay.

871
00:31:36,510 --> 00:31:38,410
Let's exchange numbers...

872
00:31:38,780 --> 00:31:39,979
so that we can enjoy a ride together.

873
00:31:39,980 --> 00:31:41,409
That sounds good. I'm honored.

874
00:31:41,410 --> 00:31:42,510
Please give me your number.

875
00:31:43,750 --> 00:31:46,250
I'll go home and brag about what happened.

876
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:47,920
It's an honor for the entire family.

877
00:31:49,220 --> 00:31:50,450
Don't I have a good number?

878
00:31:51,420 --> 00:31:52,489
Yes, you do.

879
00:31:52,490 --> 00:31:53,920
Tae Hwan, thank you.

880
00:31:54,090 --> 00:31:55,660
I'm becoming less nervous.

881
00:31:56,030 --> 00:31:57,089
That's good to hear.

882
00:31:57,090 --> 00:31:58,760
I'm glad to help.

883
00:31:59,260 --> 00:32:01,230
Where do you want to go for a ride?

884
00:32:01,460 --> 00:32:04,630
Me? I want to go to the Namhansanseong Fortress.

885
00:32:05,170 --> 00:32:06,540
Why? To eat boiled chicken?

886
00:32:06,870 --> 00:32:08,100
While boiled chicken is nice,

887
00:32:08,440 --> 00:32:10,370
I like speeding.

888
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:11,809
Paldang is a great destination.

889
00:32:11,810 --> 00:32:13,340
- Paldang? - Let's go to Paldang.

890
00:32:13,610 --> 00:32:14,880
How much can you eat?

891
00:32:15,250 --> 00:32:16,349
How many packets of ramyeon can you eat?

892
00:32:16,350 --> 00:32:18,420
- I can eat five packets. - Really?

893
00:32:18,480 --> 00:32:20,050
I eat more than I look.

894
00:32:21,420 --> 00:32:23,019
Do you mean it? Don't overestimate yourself.

895
00:32:23,020 --> 00:32:25,059
- I eat a lot. - I eat a lot too.

896
00:32:25,060 --> 00:32:27,989
Okay. Let's go there together to celebrate...

897
00:32:27,990 --> 00:32:30,190
- passing the test, Tae Hwan. - Okay. Let's do that.

898
00:32:30,330 --> 00:32:32,430
I would've passed if I had someone like him.

899
00:32:32,530 --> 00:32:34,170
Lee Jung, what kind of an excuse is that?

900
00:32:36,930 --> 00:32:38,399
- Brother, let's watch it together. - Okay.

901
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:39,499
Hello.

902
00:32:39,500 --> 00:32:42,209
Go over the rules with us.

903
00:32:42,210 --> 00:32:44,530
(They get an instructional video before the driving test.)

904
00:32:45,010 --> 00:32:46,339
It's my third time watching it.

905
00:32:46,340 --> 00:32:48,526
- They look good together. - They're like father and son.

906
00:32:48,550 --> 00:32:49,579
It's your first time, right?

907
00:32:49,580 --> 00:32:50,609
- Yes. - It's my third time.

908
00:32:50,610 --> 00:32:51,920
(Laughing)

909
00:32:52,550 --> 00:32:53,550
(Nervous)

910
00:32:53,551 --> 00:32:55,720
(Fine)

911
00:32:55,920 --> 00:32:58,020
You'll be able to pass, so don't be nervous.

912
00:32:58,090 --> 00:32:59,690
- You look nervous. - I was nervous.

913
00:32:59,860 --> 00:33:01,689
You become more nervous with time. You need to take it right away.

914
00:33:01,690 --> 00:33:03,971
- I know. That's the difference. - That's right. I agree.

915
00:33:04,130 --> 00:33:05,399
Please pick up your belongings...

916
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:06,700
and head outside.

917
00:33:07,500 --> 00:33:09,000
What is he going to do?

918
00:33:10,230 --> 00:33:11,430
Take it with you.

919
00:33:12,100 --> 00:33:14,000
- Tae Hwan, let's go together. - Let's go.

920
00:33:15,540 --> 00:33:17,769
- Let's go. - This is making my heart beat fast.

921
00:33:17,770 --> 00:33:18,839
You know that feeling, right?

922
00:33:18,840 --> 00:33:22,380
I totally know that feeling. Seriously.

923
00:33:23,710 --> 00:33:26,250
(It's time to reap the fruit of his hard work.)

924
00:33:28,080 --> 00:33:30,519
(This is the battlefield.)

925
00:33:30,520 --> 00:33:31,590
Look at the curved route.

926
00:33:32,220 --> 00:33:33,589
You'll know if you've tried out...

927
00:33:33,590 --> 00:33:35,236
for the Class Two Small Motorcycle License.

928
00:33:35,260 --> 00:33:38,090
The track reminds me of tightroping...

929
00:33:38,330 --> 00:33:41,330
because it's incredibly narrow.

930
00:33:41,430 --> 00:33:43,430
It looks like it's this wide.

931
00:33:44,770 --> 00:33:46,800
(Curved course)

932
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:48,969
- It's narrow. - It's narrow indeed.

933
00:33:48,970 --> 00:33:50,440
(S-curve course)

934
00:33:50,770 --> 00:33:52,156
Even when it's straight... Look at that.

935
00:33:52,180 --> 00:33:53,309
I think that'll be easy.

936
00:33:53,310 --> 00:33:54,979
That's the course I could mess up.

937
00:33:54,980 --> 00:33:56,209
I think the same about that course.

938
00:33:56,210 --> 00:33:57,279
- This course is fine. - That's right.

939
00:33:57,280 --> 00:33:58,320
- It's easy. - Totally.

940
00:34:01,520 --> 00:34:04,720
(Only one mistake is allowed.)

941
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:07,760
(I'm nervous.)

942
00:34:08,190 --> 00:34:09,659
We'll begin the driving test for small motorcycles.

943
00:34:09,660 --> 00:34:11,230
The first one is Park Tae Hwan.

944
00:34:12,100 --> 00:34:13,159
(Tae Hwan goes first.)

945
00:34:13,160 --> 00:34:15,146
- My goodness. - Sung Hwan's friend will go first.

946
00:34:15,170 --> 00:34:16,270
Tae Hwan.

947
00:34:16,670 --> 00:34:17,770
(Hugging)

948
00:34:17,870 --> 00:34:19,569
- I'll do well. - He's confident.

949
00:34:19,570 --> 00:34:20,839
- Oh, my. - We have elbow pads here.

950
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:22,170
- I'll do well. - Okay.

951
00:34:22,340 --> 00:34:24,770
(Meanwhile, his legs go weak from being nervous.)

952
00:34:24,970 --> 00:34:26,440
Put them on.

953
00:34:26,780 --> 00:34:28,580
- I'll hold on to it. - Thank you.

954
00:34:29,510 --> 00:34:31,920
(I feel nervous.)

955
00:34:33,980 --> 00:34:35,790
This is driving me crazy.

956
00:34:37,550 --> 00:34:40,920
It looks like Tae Hwan is certain that he'll pass.

957
00:34:41,290 --> 00:34:42,789
Please get on the motorcycle.

958
00:34:42,790 --> 00:34:43,890
Please get on.

959
00:34:44,460 --> 00:34:46,629
(I'll show you, Sung Hwan.)

960
00:34:46,630 --> 00:34:49,599
I don't know what to think about him. I'm a bit anxious.

961
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:52,200
I think he'll pass very easily.

962
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:53,939
- We can't say that for sure. - Really?

963
00:34:53,940 --> 00:34:55,439
- To be honest, I'm not certain. - Really?

964
00:34:55,440 --> 00:34:57,840
I think he'll pass since he can eat five packets of ramyeon.

965
00:34:58,240 --> 00:34:59,840
He's experienced.

966
00:35:00,340 --> 00:35:01,440
Tae Hwan, good luck.

967
00:35:01,780 --> 00:35:02,850
Tae Hwan, good luck.

968
00:35:04,650 --> 00:35:06,779
Park Tae Hwan, raise your right hand if you're ready.

969
00:35:06,780 --> 00:35:08,180
(Raising)

970
00:35:08,420 --> 00:35:09,490
Let's go.

971
00:35:16,798 --> 00:35:19,037
Park Tae Hwan, raise your right hand if you're ready.

972
00:35:19,038 --> 00:35:20,298
(Raising)

973
00:35:20,638 --> 00:35:21,668
Let's go.

974
00:35:29,548 --> 00:35:32,748
(He steps on the gas without hesitation.)

975
00:35:33,578 --> 00:35:34,887
(Lightning-fast start)

976
00:35:34,888 --> 00:35:36,618
- He's driving so fast. - He's...

977
00:35:36,748 --> 00:35:38,487
- I'm nervous. - I think he'll pass.

978
00:35:38,488 --> 00:35:41,528
- He's driving so fast. - He's either the best driver...

979
00:35:41,828 --> 00:35:42,988
or a complete newbie.

980
00:35:43,358 --> 00:35:46,028
I've never heard that engine sound at a driving test center.

981
00:35:46,458 --> 00:35:48,298
He stepped on the gas.

982
00:35:48,628 --> 00:35:50,128
(Speeding up)

983
00:35:53,038 --> 00:35:54,438
You have gone away from the course.

984
00:35:54,638 --> 00:35:55,808
(Oh, no.)

985
00:35:56,208 --> 00:35:57,414
You have gone away from the course.

986
00:35:57,438 --> 00:35:58,538
What?

987
00:35:59,338 --> 00:36:01,448
(Due to the speed, he goes off course.)

988
00:36:01,648 --> 00:36:03,207
Why is he going so fast?

989
00:36:03,208 --> 00:36:04,307
(Is he in a hurry?)

990
00:36:04,308 --> 00:36:06,778
Did he think he needed to speed to get the points?

991
00:36:07,148 --> 00:36:08,247
"Do I need to speed?"

992
00:36:08,248 --> 00:36:09,618
He wanted to show Sung Hwan.

993
00:36:09,818 --> 00:36:11,287
- "I can ride pretty well." - Yes.

994
00:36:11,288 --> 00:36:13,187
- "I'll show you, Sung Hwan." - I bet he did that.

995
00:36:13,188 --> 00:36:15,388
- "I'll show you." Vroom. - Vroom.

996
00:36:16,288 --> 00:36:17,387
You have gone away from the course.

997
00:36:17,388 --> 00:36:18,948
(He loses points as soon as he begins.)

998
00:36:19,228 --> 00:36:20,628
You have gone away from the course.

999
00:36:22,028 --> 00:36:24,508
(He needs to complete the course without making any mistakes.)

1000
00:36:25,338 --> 00:36:27,238
Points deducted for stepping on the ground.

1001
00:36:28,868 --> 00:36:30,588
Points deducted for stepping on the ground.

1002
00:36:30,768 --> 00:36:32,808
You have failed to meet the minimum score.

1003
00:36:33,578 --> 00:36:34,677
Where are you going?

1004
00:36:34,678 --> 00:36:35,807
Hey.

1005
00:36:35,808 --> 00:36:37,107
(This is insane.)

1006
00:36:37,108 --> 00:36:40,317
- What is he going to do? - He showed us what not to do.

1007
00:36:40,318 --> 00:36:41,838
("The Art of Faults" by Park Tae Hwan)

1008
00:36:42,948 --> 00:36:44,387
(Shouting)

1009
00:36:44,388 --> 00:36:46,258
Points deducted for stepping on the ground.

1010
00:36:46,418 --> 00:36:48,358
You have failed to meet the minimum score.

1011
00:36:48,558 --> 00:36:49,727
You have failed to meet the minimum score.

1012
00:36:49,728 --> 00:36:52,728
(What's up with him?)

1013
00:36:53,028 --> 00:36:55,368
(A strong man who doesn't need to practice)

1014
00:36:55,568 --> 00:36:57,998
(I'll pass in 1 go.)

1015
00:36:58,298 --> 00:36:59,398
Get off.

1016
00:36:59,698 --> 00:37:01,067
- For real? - It's over.

1017
00:37:01,068 --> 00:37:02,168
"For real?"

1018
00:37:03,008 --> 00:37:04,067
"For real?"

1019
00:37:04,068 --> 00:37:05,628
(He suddenly asked if it was for real.)

1020
00:37:06,778 --> 00:37:08,277
You really become that way.

1021
00:37:08,278 --> 00:37:11,077
You become so confused once you fail.

1022
00:37:11,078 --> 00:37:12,948
- I mean... - He misspoke...

1023
00:37:13,048 --> 00:37:14,247
- since he was flustered. - It happens.

1024
00:37:14,248 --> 00:37:15,388
"For real?"

1025
00:37:17,518 --> 00:37:18,588
Get off.

1026
00:37:18,958 --> 00:37:20,188
- For real? - It's over.

1027
00:37:20,818 --> 00:37:23,288
(Tae Hwan suddenly becomes small.)

1028
00:37:23,388 --> 00:37:26,028
Please begin after listening to the verbal instructions.

1029
00:37:26,528 --> 00:37:27,627
Well done.

1030
00:37:27,628 --> 00:37:29,097
(Embarrassed)

1031
00:37:29,098 --> 00:37:30,127
Look at that facial expression.

1032
00:37:30,128 --> 00:37:31,198
Well done.

1033
00:37:32,168 --> 00:37:33,238
It's hard.

1034
00:37:34,598 --> 00:37:35,668
He's cute.

1035
00:37:35,808 --> 00:37:37,067
- It's okay. - It's hard.

1036
00:37:37,068 --> 00:37:39,678
- You get nervous when you go first. - It's so scary.

1037
00:37:40,008 --> 00:37:41,078
It's so scary.

1038
